  "solution": "Given:\n\nx = √ 2 + 1 and y = frac{{√ 2 }}{3}, \n\nConcept used:\n\na³ - b³ = (a - b)(a² + ab + b²)\n\n(a - b)² = a² - 2ab + b²\n\nCalculation:\n\n(x - 2y - 1)(x2 + 4y2 + 2xy - 2x - 2y + 1)\n\n⇒ {(x - 1) - 2y}{(x² - 2x + 1) + (2y)² + (2xy - 2y)}\n\n⇒ {(x - 1) - 2y}{(x2 - 2x + 1) + (2y)2 + 2y(x - 1)}\n\n⇒ {(x - 1) - 2y}{(x - 1)² + (2y)2 + 2y(x - 1)}\n\n⇒ (x - 1)³ - (2y)³\n\n⇒ (√2 + 1 - 1)³ - ({2√2 over 3})³\n\n⇒ 2√2 - frac{{16sqrt 2 }}{{27}}\n\n⇒ frac{{38sqrt 2 }}{{27}}\n\n**∴ The value of (x - 2y - 1)(x2 + 4y2 + 2xy - 2x - 2y + 1) is frac{{38sqrt 2 }}{{27}}.**\n\n4f:T",
